# Bot-blocked or unstable hosts: valid in a browser, rejected by the checker.
linkedin\.com
x\.com
twitter\.com
private-eye\.co\.uk
# PNAS is reached through a DOI, and lychee matches the URL as written in the
# source rather than the redirect target, so the DOI form is what must be excluded.
# Kept to the one article, so that a mistyped PNAS DOI still fails the check.
# No bare pnas\.org pattern is needed for the files linkcheck.yml actually scans.
# bibliography.md does carry a legacy www.pnas.org/cgi/content URL that would very
# likely fail, but that file is not in the scanned list; adding it would need this
# exclusion widened rather than the URL being assumed absent.
doi\.org/10\.1073/pnas\.2512930123
